      "ok": true,
      "answer": "Here's how **long rests** work in Frosthaven:\n\n**Declaring a Long Rest**\nDuring the **Card Selection** step, instead of playing two cards, a character may declare a long rest — but only if they have **at least two cards in their discard pile**. A long rest constitutes their **entire turn** for the round and is performed on **initiative 99**.\n\n**Long Rest Steps (in order):**\n1. **Lose one card of their choice** from their discard pile and return the remaining cards to their hand. *(mandatory)*\n2. **Perform *Heal 2*, self.** *(optional)*\n3. **Recover all spent items.** Items can even be used during the same turn they are recovered. *(optional)*\n\n> *Rulebook, p. 38*\n\n**Key points:**\n- The character plays no ability cards that round — the long rest *is* their turn.\n- Unlike a short rest, you **choose** which card to lose (rather than losing one at random).\n- Because initiative is 99, long-resting characters act **last** in the round order.",
